ADDENDA <Act No. 16710, Dec. 3, 2019>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of subparagraph 7b of Article 10, and Article 41-2 shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to Restrictions on Activities in Restricted Areas for Conversion or Temporary Use of Mountainous Districts)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraph 7b of Article 10, the previous provisions shall apply where an application for consultation, permission, or reporting falling under any of the following subparagraphs is filed with the Minister of the Korea Forest Service, etc. to install solar energy facilities before this Act enters into force:
1. Consultation on designation, etc. of areas, districts, zones, etc. under Article 8;
2. Permission for temporary use of mountainous districts, permission for change, or reporting on change under Article 15-2.
Article 3 (Applicability to Entities Engaged in Renewable Energy Power Generation Business)
The amended provisions of Article 41-2 shall begin to apply where an application for consultation, permission, or reporting falling under any of the following cases is filed after the same amended provisions enter into force:
1. Consultation on designation, etc. of areas, districts, zones, etc. under Article 8;
2. Permission for temporary use of mountainous districts, permission for change, or reporting on change under Article 15-2.

